# GitHub governance (kami-community/kami)

## People

| GitHub | Role today | Review / merge |
|---|---|---|
| `@saranambiar` | Org admin, repo admin | Can approve Varad's PRs; **cannot approve her own** |
| `@VaradDurge` | Org member, repo **write** | Can approve Sara's PRs; **cannot approve his own**; cannot change rulesets, secrets, or GitHub Apps |

Either maintainer's approving review satisfies the required-review rule. Request the other person as reviewer on every PR.

## CODEOWNERS

`.github/CODEOWNERS` assigns `*` (and legal/automation paths) to both people. Do not add a third owner without an explicit maintainer decision. Do not require *both* approvals unless they change branch protection.

## Cursor Bugbot

Bugbot is **off** for this repo. Do not re-enable it. Do not `@cursor review` / `bugbot run` on PRs. Use human review. `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` tells Bugbot to skip if it still fires.

Disable in the Cursor dashboard (repo toggle) if comments still appear: https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot — Sara (admin / whoever installed the GitHub App) may need to flip it.

## PRs

- Base branch is `dev` (not `main`), except hotfixes.
- CLA bot must pass on contributor PRs after `.github/workflows/cla.yml` is on `dev`.
- Do not commit secrets. Do not add `Co-authored-by: Claude` / similar AI trailers.
